  "source_read_notes": [
    "All selected passages were read as complete retained source units; headings, conditions, examples, notes, citations and cross-page text remain unchanged. Selection claims are project-authored; machine boundaries remain unresolved and specialist review has not occurred.",
    "DMG 64007 distinguishes components of the industrial scheme; receipt of basic IIDB does not itself assert entitlement to every component. The REA accident/disease restrictions, retained US dates and CAA conditions are kept explicit.",
    "The frozen US wording differs: DMG 64020 says no new claims could be made from 8.4.87, while DMG 28065 and 51033 say the supplement was removed from the scheme on 6.4.87 but could continue in payment. Preserve both dates and descriptions as potentially different events; do not silently normalise them to a single closure date.",
    "DMG 71099 permits the source RP/IIDB/REA pairing with restrictions; the REA/RA transition is a different question from basic IIDB at pension age. DMG 71766 and frozen-REA qualification in 71773 prevent a one-line transition answer. The six examples in 71776 span three PDF pages and remain whole.",
    "DMG 17085 is a two-page table. Original PDF pages 10 and 11 were rendered and visually inspected: the PIP daily living row is paired with CAA and specified attendance-based schemes, not every industrial benefit; the preceding RP/ESA/CA row continues across the page boundary. Text includes the original 18092 reference discrepancy.",
    "Income rules keep their chapter scope: DMG 28 is IS/JSA(IB), DMG 51 ESA(IR), ADM H5 UC. DMG 17040 expressly includes New Style JSA/ESA within its own Act-benefit overlap definition only. Presence or absence in a list is not a proof of entitlement.",
    "The PIP additional-benefit proposal is deliberately bounded to a carer-qualifying-benefit route and the no-partner PC severe-disability route; it cannot establish all associated benefits or concessions.",
    "DMG 60043 and 60044 concern one carer and multiple cared-for people, whereas 60026 concerns multiple carers and one cared-for person. Historical dates and the full election example are preserved.",
    "The CA impact profile preserves underlying entitlement versus payment and the two directions of household effect. DMG 78105 source example amounts and H5064 historical Scottish amounts are not current rates.",
    "All cited amendments, legal provisions, dependency closure and individual facts remain unresolved obligations. This authoring file is not activated by itself; a later frozen projection and guarded runtime evaluation are required."
  ]
